#
# Waveshare ESP32-P4 + ESP32-C6 co-processor over SDIO. The hosted transport
# and its pinout, the silicon revision, the main-task stack, the block-ack
# window and the PSRAM-mempool/64-byte-cache-line pair all come from
# espos/sdkconfig.d/espos.defaults.esp32p4; this file adds the BLE half.

# PSRAM on. The board has it and the gateway was brought up with it; espOS
# leaves the choice to the project (its base P4 config enables none), but its
# CONFIG_ESP_HOSTED_MEMPOOL_PREFER_SPIRAM=y depends on SPIRAM and is dropped
# silently without this line — the transport's DMA pool would then sit in the
# internal RAM the Bluetooth host stack and WiFi already share. Line mode
# (hex) and clock (200 MHz) are IDF's P4 defaults and not restated.
CONFIG_SPIRAM=y

# --- Bluedroid over the hosted VHCI ------------------------------------
# The P4 has no radio of its own: BT_CONTROLLER_DISABLED is what makes the
# host stack talk HCI to the C6 through esp_hosted instead of looking for a
# local controller.
#
# esp_hosted 3.x key names. 3.0 removed CONFIG_ESP_HOSTED_ENABLE_BT_BLUEDROID
# and CONFIG_ESP_HOSTED_BLUEDROID_HCI_VHCI, which this file set until espOS
# 0.14, and IDF drops an assignment to a symbol that no longer exists without a
# word -- so leaving them would mean a gateway that scans nothing and a build
# that went green. espOS's consumer lint fails the configure on them.
#
# The hosted side now only says "BT feature on"; which host stack is bound
# follows from CONFIG_BT_BLUEDROID_ENABLED in sdkconfig.defaults beside this
# file. Init order is still load-bearing -- the remote controller must be
# init+enabled before the HCI driver is attached, or the first use of its
# function pointers faults (verified 2026-08-21) -- but it is no longer this
# project's job: esp_hosted_bt_host_stack_setup(), which espos_ble calls after
# esp_hosted_connect_to_slave(), does both in order.
CONFIG_BT_CONTROLLER_DISABLED=y
CONFIG_ESP_HOSTED_HOST_FEAT_BT=y

# --- Network: cable when there is one, WiFi otherwise -------------------
# One image for every Waveshare P4 board. espos_eth and the WiFi station both
# start, and espOS routes over the cable whenever it has an address
# (espos/docs/net.md, "Wired Ethernet"). On the PoE-ETH board the cable
# carries the network; on the Touch-LCD 7B and X, which have no PHY, the
# Ethernet start logs and gives up and the station carries it. Until 1.0.0
# this file turned the station off, which left those boards with no network
# at all and kept the gateway off them in the registry.
#
# The provisioning portal stays down while the cable is up (espos/docs/wifi.md),
# so a PoE gateway with no stored network raises no access point. One that
# has stored credentials joins WiFi beside the cable and shares the C6 radio
# with the BLE scanner; set wifi.sta_enabled to false on it to give the radio
# to BLE alone.
